# Dev-stage build output (go build . inside installer/). The distributable
# binaries live in bin/ and ARE committed.
/installer
/installer.exe

# `go build -o bin/<existing>` leaves a `<name>~` backup on Windows when it
# replaces a binary that is still mapped. Those are byproducts, never shipped.
/bin/*~

# Windows resource object generated by go-winres (scripts/winres.ts) at build
# time; the built exe in bin/ carries the embedded manifest/icon. winres/*.png
# and winres/winres.json ARE committed (they are the source of the resource).
/rsrc_*.syso

# Staged embed payloads (intermediate build inputs, populated by build.ts /
# scripts/build-dev-installers.ts before compiling). They live beside the
# package that embeds them (internal/payload/data/) because Go resolves embed
# patterns relative to the package directory. The compiled binaries carry the
# embedded copies, so these are not committed. data/loader IS committed (it is
# the standalone loader embed, small and stable).
/internal/payload/data/chrome/
/internal/payload/data/extension/
/internal/payload/data/native-host/{linux,darwin,windows}/
